  "answer": "This has been reported before. The Command Palette low-level keyboard hook is ignored when the focused window is elevated (running as admin) or is Task Manager. That is why Win+S falls through to Windows Search. PowerToys#41229 has a maintainer saying this directly. PowerToys#39704 reports the same thing: the CmdPal shortcut stops working when an elevated app is focused, even with PowerToys running as admin and the hook enabled. PowerToys#38297 is the tracking thread for Win+S, Win+R and Win+Space support. None of these tickets gives a fix. Until one exists, you have two options. You can use a different shortcut that doesn't need the low-level hook, such as Alt+Space or the default Win+Alt+Space. Or you can click away from the admin window to a non-elevated window before pressing Win+S. Add your logs and Windows build to #39704 if you want to help the team investigate."
 },
